            <ArticleTitle>Targeting educational initiatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-52, 211</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The nursing education department of a large teaching hospital faced the challenge of prioritizing the delivery of staff education programs after reductions in personnel and resources. Patient population data were used to guide curricula development. Results included improved clinical practice in a cost-effective manner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
